{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730475Z","id":"a4a310b7720a2f36518e5fe0b5653834da6f84263bb0802677a4d15f54d6e212","body":{"detail":"Reverting this canonical(exe) (passing exe as given to upgrade_recently_failed) passes every test. The comparison in replace (line 669) is tested and covers the same case, so this one is either redundant or needs a test of its own.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":626},"end":{"line":630},"content_hash":"1d92f71c94d077b862e4845a3edce786a4f7884fcc524768cb0baaecc0ecdad0"},"suggested_fix":"Add a test where exe is a symbolic link to a recently failed upgrade's executable and connect_matching must keep the running daemon, or drop the duplicate canonicalization.","summary":"connect_matching's canonical-path comparison has no test","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/plugin_bin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730523Z","id":"ed4233fa539f102f3314b5773ae74473e5b1644a5d7689255d2b17c555a2a434","body":{"detail":"version_line allows VERSION_TIMEOUT (3 s) for --version and ignores its exit status; Pi's binaryVersion (plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts:160) also allows 3 s. The wrapper allows PROBE_SECS (5 s) and needs exit 0 (scripts/ensure-clax.sh:120, 203-210). A clax whose first run takes 3 to 5 s is run by the wrapper but called 'not clax' by doctor.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":19},"end":{"line":47},"content_hash":"a92facfc5633cabc0b2f2baf5f2521e6ddd17ddb395b9895ee2433d71d2c3397"},"suggested_fix":"Use the wrapper's rule: 5 s and exit 0.","summary":"clax doctor --agent's binary probe differs from the plugin wrapper's","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/plugin_bin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730556Z","id":"081306b9528d6182e396da2db05cc5b0e01c19cd13f8248f164617fd3270d1f5","body":{"detail":"clax_version returns None for a foreign program, a file that is not executable, a timeout, and a crash, so clax doctor --agent and clax bin (lines 214, 238, 355) cannot say which. The wrapper does (CHECK_WHY in scripts/ensure-clax.sh:203-210).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":53},"end":{"line":56},"content_hash":"08dce240c6c913454f637583c05d78519e1a32a817bd0c06aa614401e13dc1f4"},"suggested_fix":"Return the reason with the failure and print it, as the wrapper does.","summary":"'not a usable clax binary' covers four causes","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/plugin_bin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730585Z","id":"b24855544daf2081feddec3821b50ee9a81ae5b2a9bcf1fc27640a71e4ac03c3","body":{"detail":"It reads stdout only after the child exits, so a --version that leaves a background process holding stdout open makes read_to_string wait past VERSION_TIMEOUT; and on timeout only the direct child is killed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":48},"end":{"line":50},"content_hash":"711b6eb4edbc6e7e8f665352ef5abdd6798c62b7d20e6c69870055dcd822b333"},"suggested_fix":"Read stdout on a thread bounded by the deadline, or run the child in its own process group and kill the group.","summary":"version_line can block past its timeout","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730632Z","id":"c14369e54a9202d452a90bf0681100d9aed8b671e7134d6d42723d2cd5b95216","body":{"detail":"The recorded reason keeps the PID and port of the rolled-back daemon at the time of failure, which clax status and doctor print later as 'why:' (UpgradeHold::to_json, line 347), after that daemon may have stopped or moved.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":279},"end":{"line":292},"content_hash":"03fa82fd4bbe9374a21e0f9d43ed94372d5cc107ab701a879aa875f4f534c863"},"summary":"A held upgrade's reason goes stale","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731651Z","id":"b3b3ce571015a1f6d9fbc79e2d4710d2bc884944c4ae0140ebee1196bbc7078d","body":{"detail":"They are among the slowest Rust tests on purpose: they show a daemon that never answers is stopped before the rollback, and an old daemon that ignores shutdown is terminated after the grace.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1104},"end":{"line":1148},"content_hash":"ddac1a1f4587cebd33b0a7d6fee46b7838404a60aa65a0954c28e06274c2a326"},"summary":"These replacement tests wait out the real 7 s shutdown grace and 5 s readiness deadline","tags":["gate-speed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
